From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Tyshchenko <igort@vivi.io>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] tsdemux: recover at PUSI on continuity counter mismatch

GStreamer 1.26.11 (upstream commit 3a0229a7f8, gstreamer!10560) made
tsdemux drop the current packet on a continuity counter mismatch even
when it starts a new payload unit. YouTube HLS TS segments restart
their counters at every segment boundary, so the keyframe PES that
starts each segment was discarded and YTDL video melted or froze.
Restore the old recover-at-PUSI behaviour: discard any stale partial
PES header and process the packet as the start of a new PES. Remove
once upstream restores this or auto-enables the
ignore-continuity-counter property (gstreamer!11884) for HLS.
---
 subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst/mpegtsdemux/tsdemux.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst/mpegtsdemux/tsdemux.c
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst/mpegtsdemux/tsdemux.c
@@ -3869,10 +3869,21 @@
       packet->pid, packet->payload_unit_start_indicator,
       packet->scram_afc_cc & 0x30, cc, packet->payload);
 
-  /* Check continuity */
+  /* Check continuity.
+   *
+   * A mismatch is fatal, except if this packet starts a new payload unit
+   * (from which we can recover): any stale partial PES header is dropped,
+   * the pending payload is flushed downstream by the
+   * payload_unit_start_indicator handling below, and this packet is
+   * processed as the start of a new PES. This matches the behaviour of
+   * gst_ts_demux_queue_data() up to 1.24, and is required for streams whose
+   * continuity counters restart at (self-contained) segment boundaries,
+   * e.g. YouTube HLS MPEG-TS segments, where dropping the packet would
+   * discard the keyframe PES that starts each segment. */
   if (stream->continuity_counter != CONTINUITY_UNSET) {
     if (((stream->continuity_counter + 1) % 16) != cc) {
-      if (stream->state != PENDING_PACKET_EMPTY) {
+      if (stream->state != PENDING_PACKET_EMPTY
+          && !packet->payload_unit_start_indicator) {
 #ifndef GST_DISABLE_GST_DEBUG
         gchar *pad_name = gst_pad_get_name (stream->pad);
         GST_ELEMENT_WARNING_WITH_DETAILS (demux, STREAM, DEMUX,
@@ -3899,6 +3910,14 @@
         stream->state = PENDING_PACKET_EMPTY;
 
         return GST_FLOW_OK;
+      } else if (stream->state != PENDING_PACKET_EMPTY
+          && G_UNLIKELY (stream->pending_header_data)) {
+        /* Recovering at a payload unit start: drop any stale partial PES
+         * header so this packet's header is parsed fresh. Pending payload
+         * is flushed downstream by the handling below. */
+        g_free (stream->pending_header_data);
+        stream->pending_header_data = NULL;
+        stream->pending_header_size = 0;
       }
     }
   }
